[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 500,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 539,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71126,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 314,
        "headingId": 539,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cellular angiofibroma is a benign fibroblastic neoplasm composed of bland spindle cells, collagenous stroma, and prominent vasculature. Other members of the angiofibroma family of tumours are myofibroblastoma and spindle cell&nbsp;/ pleomorphic lipoma, with similar morphology, immunohistochemical profiles, and molecular genetic backgrounds.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-24T17:31:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 501,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 540,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71127,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 314,
        "headingId": 540,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9160/0 Cellular angiofibroma</p>\r\n<p>8825/0 Myofibroblastoma</p>\r\n<p>8857/0 Spindle cell&nbsp;/ pleomorphic lipoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-24T17:31:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 502,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 541,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71128,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 314,
        "headingId": 541,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>EE6Y &amp; XH4E06 Other specified fibromatous disorders of skin and soft tissue &amp; Cellular angiofibroma</p>\r\n<p>EE6Y &amp; XH1JJ2 Other specified fibromatous disorders of skin and soft tissue &amp; Angiofibroma, NOS</p>\r\n<p>EE6Y &amp; XH73S9 Other specified fibromatous disorders of skin and soft tissue &amp; Giant cell angiofibroma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-24T17:31:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 503,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 542,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71129,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 314,
        "headingId": 542,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> male angiofibroblastoma-like tumour.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-24T17:31:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 504,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 543,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71130,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 314,
        "headingId": 543,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-24T17:31:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 505,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 544,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71131,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 314,
        "headingId": 544,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Angiofibroma is usually located in the superficial soft tissues of the inguinoscrotal or paratesticular area. Very rarely, angiofibroma can occur in the kidney, testis, spermatic cord, or prostate {15489646; 25105048; 20852591; 20305534}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-24T17:31:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 506,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 545,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71132,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 314,
        "headingId": 545,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The clinical features are mostly nonspecific; patients usually present with a slow-growing, painless mass. It may occasionally be associated with a hernia {15489646; 9422311}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-24T17:31:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 507,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 546,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71133,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 314,
        "headingId": 546,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Angiofibroma occurs over a wide age range in both sexes (peak incidence is in the fifth decade of life for women and the seventh decade for men), with a slight female predominance {15489646; 25105048; 20852591; 20305534; 9422311}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-24T17:31:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 508,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 547,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71134,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 314,
        "headingId": 547,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-24T17:31:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 509,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 548,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71135,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 314,
        "headingId": 548,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cellular angiofibroma shares morphological and immunohistochemical features with mammary and soft tissue myofibroblastoma and spindle cell&nbsp;/ pleomorphic lipoma. Moreover, all these tumours are characterized by a loss of genetic material from the 13q14 region (monoallelic deletion of <em>RB1</em> and <em>FOXO1</em>). Therefore, a unifying conceptual name, &ldquo;13q/<em>RB1</em> family&rdquo;, has been proposed for all these tumours {26523539; 27825811; 20852591}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-24T17:31:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 516,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 555,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71136,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 314,
        "headingId": 555,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The size ranges from 6&nbsp;to 250&nbsp;mm (median: 28&nbsp;mm in women, 70&nbsp;mm in men). Tumours usually present as well-circumscribed, oval or lobulated masses with a soft to rubbery consistency. The colour on cross-section ranges from white to grey-pink or yellow-brown {15489646; 25105048; 20852591; 20305534}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-24T17:31:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 510,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 549,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71137,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 314,
        "headingId": 549,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Angiofibroma is composed of a moderately to highly cellular proliferation of uniform short spindle cells, which are haphazardly arranged or form vague fascicular or palisading patterns. Stroma is prominent and composed of bundles of wispy collagen and small to medium-sized thick-walled vessels. A fatty component is present in about half of the cases. Hyalinization, oedema, or myxoid change is common within the stroma. Mitoses are rare. Areas with sarcomatoid transformation have been observed in rare cases {20852591}. Neoplastic cells frequently show loss of RB1 protein expression and are variably positive for CD34 and SMA. Desmin is positive in a minority of cases. In the differential diagnosis, solitary fibrous tumour has to be considered.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-24T17:31:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 511,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 550,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71138,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 314,
        "headingId": 550,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-24T17:31:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 512,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 551,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71139,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 314,
        "headingId": 551,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Analysis of the <em>RB1</em> gene, located on chromosome band 13q14, can be used to support the diagnosis {17727484; 20852591}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-24T17:31:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 515,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 554,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71140,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 314,
        "headingId": 554,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> bland spindle cells growing within a stroma composed of short bundles of wispy collagen punctuated by numerous small to medium-sized thick-walled vessels.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> a fatty component may be present; loss of RB1 protein expression may support the diagnosis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-24T17:31:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 513,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 552,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71141,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 314,
        "headingId": 552,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-24T17:31:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 514,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 553,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71142,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 314,
        "headingId": 553,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Local recurrences are rare and have mostly occurred after an incomplete excision. No metastases have been recorded.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-24T17:31:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]